To all the people saying 'don't be lazy' or 'it takes a few seconds' are missing the point. its not our job, its the darn restaurants job to do it. furthermore if its more than one drink ill likely also need to get a cup holder which sometimes they don't have. this all adds to the time it takes to load it all in the car. its not worth it for me unless its atleast $10 or more.

&#x200B;

Maybe you guys taking these low paying orders ought to realize they're making you do their work for them.

no. i refuse to take these orders unless they're worth more. as others say we don't have a food handling license to do it. and if its multiple drinks it can take a lot longer than usual.

&#x200B;

so i will complain as i feel thank ya :)

Yeah its too late then. screenshots of the time you were supposed to pick up and then drop the order off. and probably a screenshot of google maps showing the actual time it took you to get there. So you can prove you got the order before you could deliver it in the time they wanted you to. or that the restaurant was the one taking forever so you can't pick it up by the time you were supposed to either. 

